{"abstract":"Due to limited access to domain knowledge and domain-relevant benchmark data, the Container Stowage Planning Problem (CSPP) is notably under-researched. In particular, previous models of the CSPP have lacked two key aspects of the problem: lashing forces and paired block stowage. The former may reduce vessel capacity by up to 10%, and the latter is NP-hard. The Representative CSPP (RCSPP), which captures all critical aspects of the problem is formulated. The presented RCSPP incorporates overlooked constraints such as paired block stowage and lashing, along with an innovative method for estimating lashing forces, all while maintaining simplicity. A heuristic method, STOW, has been developed to identify solutions for the RCSPP using a specially designed benchmark suite based on real-world scenarios. STOW algorithm is an advanced search heuristic employing a diverse range of solution modification strategies, each tailored to address specific aspects of stowage optimization. Feasible solutions were successfully identified for all instances within the benchmark suite. Our initial findings emphasize the importance of accurately modeling lashing forces and employing paired block stowage. Results show that removing the lashing constraint can increase the number of containers stowed by over 7% on average, while disabling paired block stowage can result in nearly a 5% increase.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Agnieszka","Reinhardt, Line","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820776"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benchmark","Container stowage optimization","Heuristic search","Maritime transport","Stowage planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a representative model and benchmark suite for the container stowage planning problem","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-820776","identifier":[{"id":"105008109623","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-4d9cae5a-8d47-4759-9bc1-0568d9b2d221"],"keyword":["Benchmark","Container stowage optimization","Heuristic search","Maritime transport","Stowage planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-87DD54FB712D0D71A9D6072A209F8F6E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Programming, Logic and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Agnieszka","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"d0167f08-61c6-43c8-8716-0655ba68f4c9","name":"Sivertsen, Agnieszka","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Line","key":"reinhardtpau","last":"Reinhardt","locid":"4884f385-6ffc-42be-89ae-12e12b32d994","name":"Reinhardt, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tre.2025.104224","issn":["13665545","18785794"],"issn_org":["13665545"],"journal":"Transportation Research Part E: Logistics and Transportation Review","paperid":"104224","status":"p","title":"Transportation Research Part E: Logistics and Transportation Review","volume":"201"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105008109623"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-4d9cae5a-8d47-4759-9bc1-0568d9b2d221"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"A representative model and benchmark suite for the container stowage planning problem","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820776","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In vitro research on host–microbe interactions in the human gut has been challenging due to the differing oxygen requirements of mammalian cells and intestinal microbiota. Few models of this environment have been developed, and those available are complex, limiting the extraction of important information during experiments. Here we report an in vitro model that by simple means creates an anaerobic environment for microbiota growing on living, cultured human epithelium under physiological flow. This model enables long-term co-culture of intestinal epithelial cells with obligate anaerobic bacteria, exemplified here by Clostridioides difficile and Bacteroides fragilis. Anaerobic conditions are maintained through the integration of an anaerobization unit, developed to facilitate online deoxygenation of media via liquid-to-liquid gas diffusion, eliminating the need for encapsulation in complex gas chambers. We show that stable oxygen levels of less than 1% can be maintained in the model for several days without compromising the viability of the intestinal epithelium. Furthermore, we demonstrate the performance of the model by simulating prolonged colonization with C. difficile and B. fragilis, as well as the clinically relevant persistence of C. difficile following treatment with vancomycin.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Bang, Line L","Pettersen, Jens Sivkær","Høiland, N.","Rojek, Aleksandra Maria","Tornby, Ditte S.","Møller-Jensen, Jakob","Justesen, Ulrik Stenz","Pedersen, Rune Micha","Andersen, Thomas Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830966"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Thomas Emil"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an anaerobic in vitro flow model for studying interactions at the gastrointestinal host microbe interface","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41522-025-00800-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830966","identifier":[{"id":"40789857","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105012942856","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12340051","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-3a7de3a7-639b-4aed-87b5-90fd86a03f67"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-13829E7698A49E487E73C2D166144715"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41522-025-00800-z","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/294463094/s41522-025-00800-z.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L. L.","key":"bangpau","last":"Bang","locid":"104b74d6-8aaa-44b4-ae97-64fcf18fed5e","name":"Bang, Line L","name_org":"Bang, L. L.","orcid