ern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-00bda344-6374-4736-b315-6c4dd7f47514"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Danske politikere må forsvare EU’s succesprogram for grundforskning","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-797503","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Informed consent has been increasingly equated with standardized models and legal jargon. At Scandinavian universities, researchers are expected to adhere to European standardized models and institutional forms, necessitating documentable (preferably signed) consent from research participants. As Africanist researchers, we observe a growing dissonance between institutional expectations and fieldwork ethics and moralities. The field of African Studies has been pivotal in revealing how knowledge practices that are ostensibly universal are, in fact, products of deep-seated inequalities in higher education and knowledge production, perpetuating Western ideals of ethics. This introduction advocates for “customized consent” and introduces three concepts – consent contexts, consent interests, and consent mediators – to address and positively transform informed consent procedures and expectations.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Amanda Møller","Larsen, Rune","Jensen, Stig"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816532"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["African Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"negotiating consent in african studies a case for customized consent","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.53228/w727yg66","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816532","identifier":[{"id":"105009371460","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bb5d9973-8ce7-4f6d-9e83-8869646f6638"],"keyword":["African studies","consent contexts","consent interests","consent mediators","customized consent"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-ADB7759CCF043FFF7D5EBCFD7627B249"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.53228/w727yg66","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanda Møller","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f135b835-2fae-4dd9-bc44-45b7c5f16685","name":"Rasmussen, Amanda Møller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Rune","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Stig","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.53228/w727yg66","issn":["12354481","14599465"],"issn_org":["12354481"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nordic Journal of African Studies","pages":"71-87","publisher":"Nordic Journal of African Studies, University of Copenhagen Centre of African Studies","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of African Studies","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009371460"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bb5d9973-8ce7-4f6d-9e83-8869646f6638"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Negotiating Consent in African Studies : A Case for Customized Consent","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816532","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Reinforcement learning (RL) has shown promise in solving various combinatorial optimization problems. However, conventional RL faces challenges when dealing with real-world constraints, especially when action space feasibility is explicit and dependent on the corresponding state or trajectory. In this work, we focus on using RL in container shipping, often considered the cornerstone of global trade, by dealing with the critical challenge of master stowage planning. The main objective is to maximize cargo revenue and minimize operational costs while navigating demand uncertainty and various complex operational constraints, namely vessel capacity and stability, which must be dynamically updated along the vessel's voyage. To address this problem, we implement a deep reinforcement learning framework with feasibility projection to solve the master stowage planning problem (MPP) under demand uncertainty. The experimental results show that our architecture efficiently finds adaptive, feasible solutions for this multi-stage stochastic optimization problem, outperforming traditional mixed-integer programming and RL with feasibility regularization. Our AI-driven decision-support policy enables adaptive and feasible planning under uncertainty, optimizing operational efficiency and capacity utilization while contributing to sustainable and resilient global supply chains.","author_count":5,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Adulyasak, Yossiri","Delage, Erick","Grbic, Djordje","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828163"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","HEC Montréal"],"keyword":["Combinatorial optimization","Machine learning","Maritime logistics","Reinforcement learning","Stochastic optimization","Transportation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"navigating demand uncertainty in container shipping deep reinforcement learning for enabling adaptive and feasible master stowage planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.12756","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-828163","ids":["itu-85b71ca7-6f77-4d8b-9650-0ae57a5df79c"],"keyword":["Combinatorial optimization","Feasibility projection","Machine learning","Maritime logistics","Reinforcement learning","Transportation","stochastic optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C72F9DFF8386788C53E6658CC215FE1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2502.12756","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"hec montréal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"HEC Montréal","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yossiri","key":"adulyasakpau","last":"Adulyasak","name":"Adulyasak, Yossiri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erick","key":"delagepau","last":"Delage","name":"Delage, Erick","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Djordje","key":"grbicpau","last":"Grbic","locid":"c596539b-3ceb-497c-9a43-e71d6b0f65a6","name":"Grbic, Djordje","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-2539","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-85b71ca7-6f77-4d8b-9650-0ae57a5df79c"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Navigating Demand Uncertainty in Container Shipping: Deep Reinforcement Learning for Enabling Adaptive and Feasible Master Stowage Planning","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828163","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Adulyasak, Yossiri","Delage, Erick","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798524"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","HEC Montréal"],"keyword":["Container stowage planning","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Revenue management","Stochastic optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep reinforcement learning for revenue management under uncertainty in master stowage planning on container vessels","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108728780/25th_nmuw_program_abstracts.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798524","ids":["itu-1afa8020-96f7-4e7b-9fc2-cb0128ad5fa0"],"keyword":["Container stowage planning","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Revenue management","Stochastic optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-40BF05243DA452356DFB72C31564DB6A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108728780/25th_nmuw_program_abstracts.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, The Maritime Hub"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"hec montréal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"HEC Montréal","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yossiri","key":"adulyasakpau","last":"Adulyasak","name":"Adulyasak, Yossiri","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Erick","key":"delagepau","last":"Delage","name":"Delage, Erick","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"25th DNV Nordic Maritime Universities Workshop"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1afa8020-96f7-4e7b-9fc2-cb0128ad5fa0"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Reinforcement Learning for Revenue Management under Uncertainty in Master Stowage Planning on Container Vessels","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798524","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Workplace-based learning in surgery has developed an inherent focus on competency-based assessment tools and quantifiable skills. Trust is an essential element in the framework of Entrustable Professional Activities (EPA). However, trust is difficult to quantify and assess. Procedural variation seen among residents may be influenced by supervisors’ trust in their trainee. The objective of this study was to explore how supervisors base their trust decisions when granting autonomy to surgical residents. Methods: A constructivist grounded theory approach was used to guide interviews with specialists in general surgery at different teaching hospitals in Denmark. Results: We recruited and interviewed 19 surgeons, all of whom were specialised within general surgery. In the interviews, the informants articulated four interconnected themes that characterise the elements that supervisors employ when making trust decisions about when to grant autonomy to surgical residents: (1) approach, (2) relational skills and competencies, (3) departmental solidarity, and (4) technical skills and knowing own limits. On the basis of these four categories, we created the acronym ARTS. Conclusion: ARTS may provide a point of departure for critical discourse on the criteria that should inform decisions regarding the granting of autonomy, as well as the essential components that ought to be integrated into assessment frameworks.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hesseldal, Karen Busk","Møller, Jane Ege","Paltved, Charlotte","Madsen, Anders Husted","Jensen, Rune Dall"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-816643"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hesseldal, Karen Busk"],"keyword":["Assessment","Surgical education"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the arts of being a surgeon a qualitative study exploring supervisors trust decisions when granting autonomy to trainees","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12909-025-07326-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-816643","identifier":[{"id":"40457358","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12131605","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105007102300","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ca6b0d49-653e-4996-90a7-22e673a3cc9e"],"keyword":["Assessment","Entrustment","Resident autonomy","Surgical education"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-88B08771A0B9FDACA1E843F18B7BE1DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12909-025-07326-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinical Skills Laboratory","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Mave- og Tarmkirurgi, RHG"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen Busk","key":"hesseldalpau","last":"Hesseldal","locid":"a79aba24-9562-481d-834e-df4d1d00d36e","name":"Hesseldal, Karen Busk","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jane Ege","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"b4240f2f-e323-4f28-b11c-1a603b6f9b70","name":"Møller, Jane Ege","orcid":"0000-0003-2661-0256","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"paltvedpau","last":"Paltved","locid":"0d936f91-a209-44cf-8266-0bd9b128bd43","name":"Paltved, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Husted","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"fadf30da-6cbc-427e-ae16-72d99c1ac48d","name":"Madsen, Anders Husted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rune Dall","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b210a9eb-ebe0-4b59-ae61-97a49861a7c6","name":"Jensen, Rune Dall","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40457358"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12909-025-07326-0","issn":["14726920"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Medical Education","paperid":"823","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Medical Education","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105007102300"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ca6b0d49-653e-4996-90a7-22e673a3cc9e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The ARTS of being a surgeon : a qualitative study exploring supervisors’ trust decisions when granting autonomy to trainees","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-816643","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"A crucial role of container shipping is maximizing container uptake onto vessels, optimizing the efficiency of a fundamental part of the global supply chain. In practice, liner shipping companies include block stowage patterns that ensure that containers in above and below deck partitions of bays have the same destination. Despite preventing restows, increasing free space, and benefits for crane makespan and hydrostatics, this practical planning requirement is rarely included in stowage optimization models. In our paper, we introduce a novel 0-1 IP model that searches in the space of valid paired block stowage patterns, named template planning, which ensures sufficient vessel capacity and limits to crane makespan, trim, and bending moment. Our results show that template planning outperforms traditional allocation planning concerning optimality and runtime efficiency while preserving a sufficiently accurate representation of master planning constraints and objectives.","author_count":7,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Sivertsen, Agnieszka","Jensen, Rune Møller","Andersen, Kent Høj","Garrido, Alexander","Paternina, Carlos","Voß, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776461"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCL","title":"International Conference on Computational Logistics"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, Central","America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Mexico","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","San Diego State University","Tecnológico de Monterrey","University of Hamburg"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Container stowage planning","Integer programming","Maritime logistics","Mathematical modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Sealytix"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an efficient integer programming model for solving the master planning problem of container vessel stowage","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-71993-6_16","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776461","identifier":[{"id":"85205093516","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f7fa485f-93db-4c73-9c7d-3081538c5a96"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Container stowage planning","Integer programming","Maritime logistics","Mathematical modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-C5F191EECEB7416B3CA6F930F6868E91"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-71993-6_16","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107050327/2408.08224v1.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Sealytix"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"mx","key":"tecnológico de monterrey","loc":["Mexico","America, Central","OECD"],"name":"Tecnológico de Monterrey","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"san diego state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"San Diego State University","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"de","key":"university of hamburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hamburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Agnieszka","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","name":"Sivertsen, Agnieszka","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Kent Høj","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kent Høj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"garridoped","last":"Garrido","name":"Garrido, Alexander","rank":5,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos","key":"paterninaped","last":"Paternina","name":"Paternina, Carlos","rank":6,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"voßped","last":"Voß","name":"Voß, Stefan","rank":7,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-71993-6_16","eisbn":["9783031719936_16"],"isbn":["9783031719936_16"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"236-253","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Computational Logistics","volume":"15168"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205093516"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f7fa485f-93db-4c73-9c7d-3081538c5a96"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Efficient Integer Programming Model for Solving the Master Planning Problem of Container Vessel Stowage","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776461","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Container shipping drives the global economy and is an eco-friendly mode of transportation. A key objective is to maximize the utilization of vessels, which is challenging due to the NP-hardness of stowage planning. This article surveys the literature on the Container Stowage Planning Problem (CSPP). We introduce a classification scheme to analyze single-port and multi-port CSPPs, as well as the hierarchical decomposition of CSPPs into the master and slot planning problem. Our survey shows that the area has a relatively small number of publications and that it is hard to evaluate the industrial applicability of many of the proposed solution methods due to the oversimplification of problem formulations. To address this issue, we propose a research agenda with directions for future work, including establishing a representative problem definition and providing new benchmark instances where needed.","author_count":4,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Sivertsen, Agnieszka","Pacino, Dario","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S03-095.92-768500"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Pacino, Dario"],"keyword":["Benchmarks","Container stowage planning","Literature survey","OR in maritime industry"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"literature survey on the container stowage planning problem","src":["dtu","itu","ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-RUC"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejor.2023.12.018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-095.92-768500","identifier":[{"id":"85180597797","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f2b36655-28fa-4aee-ab6b-43c