ponding":null,"first":"Peter Marcus","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Peter Marcus","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["25970127"],"newspaper":"Altinget","status":"p","title":"Altinget"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-f25b5886-77e5-492f-b153-5ee2230343e0","dtu-4281dcc9-f7c1-4f75-93ee-ac06b20ecbac","ruc-204843b5-94eb-4f45-88d2-4500cd5d13bd"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","DTU Technical University of Denmark","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Unge forskere : Regeringens forskningsstrategi er som et afsnit af skærmtrolden Hugo","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-090.80-704433","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This paper studies the Quay Crane Scheduling Problem (QCSP). The QCSP determines how a number of quay cranes should be scheduled in order to service a vessel with minimum makespan. Previous work considers the QCSP to be a combinatorially hard problem. For that reason, the focus has been on developing efficient heuristics. Our study shows, however, that the QCSP is tractable in the realistic setting, where quay cranes can share the workload of bays. We introduce a novel linear time algorithm that solves the QCSP and prove its correctness.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Herup, Mathias Offerlin","Thiesgaard, Gustav Christian Wichmann","van Twiller, Jaike","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382253"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computational complexity","Container terminals","Quay crane scheduling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a linear time algorithm for optimal quay crane scheduling","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90345620/A_linear_time_scheduling_algorithm_for_container_terminal_quay_cranes_with_minimum_makespan_PAPER.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382253","identifier":[{"id":"85138779090","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-427a3428-e70d-41c1-a594-51f5be0dd4a6"],"keyword":["Computational complexity","Container terminals","Quay crane scheduling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AAE907DCEDDF99D24C7C961F03B56FBF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90345620/A_linear_time_scheduling_algorithm_for_container_terminal_quay_cranes_with_minimum_makespan_PAPER.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Offerlin","key":"heruppau","last":"Herup","name":"Herup, Mathias Offerlin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gustav Christian Wichmann","key":"thiesgaardpau","last":"Thiesgaard","name":"Thiesgaard, Gustav Christian Wichmann","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-16579-5_5","pages":"60-73","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","subtitle":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","title":"International Conference on Computational Logistics","volume":"13557"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138779090"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-427a3428-e70d-41c1-a594-51f5be0dd4a6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Linear Time Algorithm for Optimal Quay Crane Scheduling","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382253","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Container vessel stowage planning concerns itself with placing containers on port load lists onto vessels. A stowage plan can be decomposed in master bay planning to assign cargo to general areas and slot planning to place cargo into slots of bays [1]. The goal is to maximize vessel utilization on the fronthaul and minimize operational costs by creating robust stowage plans [1]. Due to stowage and seaworthiness rules, this optimization problem belongs to the class of NP-hard problems [1]. The first phase of another hierarchically decomposed NP-hard problem has recently been solved through deep reinforcement learning (DRL), which performs well on large and complex unseen instances [2]. To our knowledge, there is one piece of work on DRL for stowage optimization, which solves an incomplete slot planning problem with a single port of discharge and uniform containers [3]. Hence, novel DRL formulations are necessary to efficiently solve realistic and unseen instances. This paper will experiment with DRL by formulating the master bay planning problem (MBP) as a finite Markov decision process, which is defined in terms of states, i.e. load lists, bay traits and capacities, and remaining cargo onboard, actions, i.e. allocating containers to bays, and rewards, i.e. total stowage cost, capacity utilization on fronthaul, and satisfying seaworthiness and stowage rules. As container allocation has no direct reward, a neural net is used to prescribe appropriate actions. Iteratively, the agent searches for an optimal policy that maximizes rewards through Markovian decision-making, whereafter network parameters are updated by proximal policy optimization. This stochastic on-policy method limits the risk of disrupting changes to solutions. Furthermore, a simulation environment will enable learning from unobserved problem instances. If DRL scales well for MBP, this opens a new venue for stowage research. We recognize sufficient data on vessel types, stacking rules in slot planning, and revenue management in stowage plans as future challenges. However, we believe that more AI research advances the field toward fully automated stowage planning.","author_count":2,"contributors":["van Twiller, Jaike","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384611"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Container Stowage","Deep reinforcement learning","Maritime logistics","Markov decision process","Master Bay Planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep reinforcement learning for master bay planning on container vessels","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eventum.upf.edu/_files/_event/_78123/_editorFiles/file/BOA2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384611","ids":["itu-e2faf9d5-06da-4b56-bc95-1d2a9ab9d559"],"keyword":["Container Stowage","Deep Reinforcement Learning","Maritime Logistics","Markov Decision Process","Master Bay Planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-97CF058F6C215F1681518C8556BABA2A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eventum.upf.edu/_files/_event/_78123/_editorFiles/file/BOA2022.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jaike","key":"vantwillerpau","last":"van Twiller","locid":"fa03d816-cd99-4fea-b45b-efe7ecd3cb0a","name":"van Twiller, Jaike","orcid":"0000-0001-8390-1629","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e2faf9d5-06da-4b56-bc95-1d2a9ab9d559"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Deep Reinforcement Learning for Master Bay Planning on Container Vessels","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384611","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
