{"abstract":"Growth differentiating factor 15 (GDF15) is expressed in the intestine and is one of the most recently identified satiety peptides. The mechanisms controlling its secretion are unclear. The present study investigated whether plasma GDF15 concentrations are meal-related and if potential responses depend on macronutrient type or are affected by previous bariatric surgery. The study included: (1) volunteers ingesting rapidly vs. slowly digested carbohydrates (sucrose vs. isomaltose) (n=10), (2) volunteers who had undergone Roux-en-Y Gastric bypass (RYGB) or sleeve gastrectomy (SG) surgery and unoperated matched controls ingesting a liquid mixed meal (n=9-10 in each group), and (3) individuals with previous RYGB compared with unoperated controls ingesting isocaloric glucose, fat or protein (n=6 in each group). Plasma was collected after an overnight fast and up to 6 h after ingestion (≥12 timepoints). In cohort 1, fasting GDF15 concentrations were ~480 pg/ml. Concentrations after sucrose or isomaltose intake did not differ from baseline (P=0.26-P>0.99) and total area-under-the-curves (tAUCs were similar between groups (P=0.77). In cohort 2, fasting GDF15 concentrations were (pg/ml): RYGB=540±41.4, SG=477±36.4, and controls=590±41.8, with no between-group differences (P=0.73). Concentrations did not increase at any postprandial time point (over all time factor: P=0.10) and tAUCs were similar between groups (P=0.73). In cohort 3, fasting plasma GDF15 was similar among the groups (P>0.99) and neither glucose, fat or protein intake consistently increased the concentrations. In conclusion, we find that plasma GDF15 was not stimulated by meal intake, and that fasting concentrations did not differ between RYGB, SG and BMI-matched controls when investigated during the weight stable phase after RYGB and SG.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Martinussen, Christoffer","Svane, Maria S.","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","Jensen, Christian Zinck","Kristiansen, Viggo B","Bookout, Angie Lynn","Jorgensen, Sebastian B","Holst, Jens Juul","Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","Madsbad, Sten","Kuhre, Rune Ehrenreich"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-438576"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma gdf000000000015 levels are similar between subjects after bariatric surgery and matched controls and are unaffected by meals","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-438576","identifier":[{"id":"34370594","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000696722500001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85116510573","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4bb44df1-2157-436c-80e5-a5d5fa208c68"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D587065101D33F2C7EB5A4C1FA13E2F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christoffer","key":"martinussenpau","last":"Martinussen","locid":"4f245fbb-67ec-4135-a359-b0f73db977a3","name":"Martinussen, Christoffer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria S.","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","locid":"4cc109fb-b416-4327-a1bd-c980486fa717","name":"Svane, Maria S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kirstine N","key":"bojsenmøllerpau","last":"Bojsen-Møller","name":"Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Zinck","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d660c7ce-532e-4c68-8105-ea678f0edade","name":"Jensen, Christian Zinck","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viggo B","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Viggo B","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Angie Lynn","key":"bookoutpau","last":"Bookout","name":"Bookout, Angie Lynn","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sebastian B","key":"jorgensenpau","last":"Jorgensen","name":"Jorgensen, Sebastian B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens J","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"864b6401-9024-4773-9bdb-f4d4ca57dcad","name":"Holst, Jens Juul","name_org":"Holst, Jens J","orcid":"0000-0001-6853-3805","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolai J.","key":"weweralbrechtsenpau","last":"Wewer Albrechtsen","locid":"0d59b767-fdca-42a0-b879-70fb0ec55651","name":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J","name_org":"Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J.","orcid":"0000-0003-4230-5753","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sten","key":"madsbadpau","last":"Madsbad","locid":"1018c708-245a-4057-9263-074578042385","name":"Madsbad, Sten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Rune Ehrenreich","key":"kuhrepau","last":"Kuhre","locid":"10f7fde3-9f77-42eb-bbaf-6d98e6938465","name":"Kuhre, Rune Ehrenreich","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34370594"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/ajpendo.00190.2021","issn":["01931849","15221555"],"issn_org":["01931849"],"journal":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Physiology: Endocrinology and Metabolism"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85116510573"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4bb44df1-2157-436c-80e5-a5d5fa208c68"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Plasma GDF15 levels are similar between subjects after bariatric surgery and matched controls and are unaffected by meals","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-438576","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Time to pregnancy (TTP), defined as the interval of time between a couple beginning to practice unprotected intercourse and conception, is a measure of fecundity, which is an individual's biologic capacity to reproduce. Fecundity has reportedly decreased over recent decades for unknown reasons that may include lifestyle, behavioral, and environmental factors. A recent Danish twin study reported that environmental factors explained approximately 70TTP 18 months (HR, 1.46; 95 1.15-1.87), compared with those reporting a TTP of 18 months (HR, 1.24; 95 0.97-1.59) compared with those reporting a TTP of 18 months (IRR, 1.16; 95 1.00-1.35) was identified. The results of this study show that reduced fecundity was associated with increased morbidity and mortality and may be a useful marker of health and survival.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ahrenfeldt, Linda Juel","Möller, Sören","Wensink, Maarten Jan","Eisenberg, M. L.","Christensen, Kaare","Jensen, Tina Kold","Lindahl-Jacobsen, Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-640053"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ahrenfeldt, Linda Juel"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Stanford University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impaired fecundity as a marker of health and survival a danish twin cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/OGX.0000000000000982","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-640053","identifier":[{"id":"85122372029","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-e973a4e9-5313-479c-97ed-38f66a6d76f9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific