{"abstract":"Stowage planning is an NP-hard combinatorial problem concerned with loading a container vessel in a given port, such that a number of constraints regarding the physical layout of the vessel and its seaworthiness are satisfied, and a number of objectives with regard to the quality of the placement are optimized. State-of-the-art methods decompose the problem into phases, the latter of which, known as slot planning, involves loading the containers into slots of a bay. This article presents an efficient matheuristic for the slot planning problem. Matheuristics are algorithms using mathematical programming techniques within a heuristic framework. The method finds solutions for 96% of 236 instances based on real stowage plans, 90% of them optimally, with an average optimality gap of 4.34% given a limit of one second per instance. This is an improvement over the results provided by previous works.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Korach, Aleksandra","Brouer, Berit Dangaard","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383466"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Large Neighbourhood Search","Matheuristics","OR in maritime industry","Slot planning","Stowage planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Optivation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"matheuristics for slot planning of container vessel bays","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84805522/ArticleBody.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383466","identifier":[{"id":"85076522181","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-95d7b8ad-ca0e-4917-b28d-ae549e3d22fb"],"keyword":["Large Neighbourhood Search","Matheuristics","OR in Maritime Industry","Slot Planning","Stowage Planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0031F6D5B1299FC776E5DECA66DE1F64"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84805522/ArticleBody.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Optivation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandra","key":"korachpau","last":"Korach","name":"Korach, Aleksandra","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Berit Dangaard","key":"brouerpau","last":"Brouer","name":"Brouer, Berit Dangaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejor.2019.09.042","issn":["03772217","18726860"],"issn_org":["03772217"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Operational Research","pages":"873-885","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Operational Research","volume":"282"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076522181"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-95d7b8ad-ca0e-4917-b28d-ae549e3d22fb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Matheuristics for Slot Planning of Container Vessel Bays","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383466","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: From the prevalent round of the Danish FIT-based colorectal cancer (CRC) screening program, we aimed (i) to evaluate the quality of recorded data and (ii) to characterize the colonoscopies by measuring variation in performance indicators between colonoscopists and assessing the ratio between adenoma detection rate (ADR) and polyp detection rate (PDR). MATERIALS AND METHODS: This study included screening colonoscopies performed in Central Denmark Region within 60 days of a positive FIT-result from 1 July 2015 through 30 June 2017. The participants were the colonoscopists, performing these procedures. The quality indicators cecal intubation rate (CIR), PDR, polyp retrieval rate (PRR), ADR and withdrawal time (WT) were evaluated. ADR/PDR ratios were calculated. RESULTS: The concordance between the recorded data and the colonoscopy reports showed Kappa values in the range of 0.47-0.97. The overall CIR was 90.6% (range 73.7%-100%), PDR: 51.9% (range 18.4%-70.2%), PRR: 94.6% (range 69.6%-100%), ADR (conventional adenomas): 50.6% (range 18.4%-70.2%), ADRx (conventional adenomas, traditional serrated adenomas and sessile serrated lesions with dysplasia): 50.9% (range 18.4%-70.2%) and the mean WT was 11.3 min (range 4.5-24.9 min). The ADR/PDR ratio was 92.8% (95% CI: 92.0%-93.6%) and the ADRx/PDR ratio was 93.2% (95% CI: 92.4%-93.9%). CONCLUSION: Data quality was generally high. We found considerable variation in performance indicators between colonoscopists reflecting the potential for improvement. Further, our findings revealed that the PDR might be a good proxy for ADR in the context of the prevalent round of FIT-based CRC screening programs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lund, Martin","Erichsen, Rune","Valori, Roland","Jensen, Thomas Møller","Njor, Sisse Helle","Laurberg, Søren","Andersen, Berit"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-269391"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["on behalf of the Central Denmark Region's \"Quality of Colonoscopies\" group†"],"corresponding_author":["Lund, Martin"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Gloucestershire Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust"],"keyword":["Adenoma detection rate","Colorectal cancer","Performance indicators","Quality indicators","Risk","Screening","Time","Withdrawal time","cecal intubation rate","fecal immunochemical test","polyp detection rate","polyp recovery","polyp retrieval rate"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"data quality and colonoscopy performance indicators in the prevalent round of a fit based colorectal cancer screening program","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85064513048","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-269391","identifier":[{"id":"000466657300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85064513048","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30978128","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f591041f-c3f2-4c56-a245-4047021190b3"],"keyword":["ADENOMA DETECTION RATE","Colorectal cancer","RISK","TIME","cecal intubation rate","fecal immunochemical test","performance indicators","polyp detection rate","polyp recovery","polyp retrieval rate","quality indicators","screening","withdrawal time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DF68C1BDB3ABEDE60FB86F9DE0B29D72"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Regional Hospital of Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"gloucestershire hospitals nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Gloucestershire Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","used":1},{"affno":3,"key":"on behalf of the central denmark region s quality of colonoscopies group","name":"on behalf of the Central Denmark Region's \"Quality of Colonoscopies\" group†","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"fb7a38f3-f3ec-4594-b215-1e297e86b311","name":"Lund, Martin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rune","key":"erichsenpau","last":"Erichsen","locid":"6ca944c9-6ee4-4ee6-abdb-3bb92452e5cc","name":"Erichsen, Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-9398-9185","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Roland","key":"valoripau","last":"Valori","name":"Valori, Roland","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"møllerjensenpau","last":"Møller Jensen","locid":"0e5e1c1c-77ef-4a30-8367-67a879935d94","name":"Jensen, Thomas Møller","name_org":"Møller Jensen, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sisse","key":"hellenjorpau","last":"Helle Njor","locid":"8cfee1bf-dfc6-4e9c-9f2d-b41621421f49","name":"Njor, Sisse Helle","name_org":"Helle Njor, Sisse","orcid":"0000-0003-0429-4176","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"laurbergpau","last":"Laurberg","locid":"fde493d2-685c-4530-8791-614babb5ff72","name":"Laurberg, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Berit","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"4f64dc11-e5ca-4037-bbad-8ca533d841e4","name":"Andersen, Berit","orcid":"0000-0003-4074-6504","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30978128"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365521.2019.1597158","issn":["00365521","15027708"],"issn_org":["00365521"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"471-477","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064513048"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f591041f-c3f2-4c56-a245-4047021190b3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Data quality and colonoscopy performance indicators in the prevalent round of a FIT-based colorectal cancer screening program","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-269391","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Energy-efficient train operation can reduce operating costs and contribute to a reduction in CO2 emissions. To utilise the full potential of energy-efficient driving, energy-efficient timetabling is crucial. To address this problem, we propose a decision support tool to give timetable planners insight into energy consumption for a given timetable. The decision support tool uses a recommendation based on quadratic optimisation of a given timetable. Differently to previous work, the optimisation uses actual data from the train operation, which is preprocessed by data reduction, outlier detection, and second-degree regression modelling. With this approach, our results show that the optimised timetables can save up to 33.07% energy on a single section and up to 6.23% for a complete timetable. Solutions are computed in less than a microsecond.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Madsen, Mathias Bejlegaard","Als, Matthias Villads Hinsch","Jensen, Rune Møller","Edinger Gram, Sune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383101"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCL","title":"International Conference on Computational Logistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Data preprocessing","Decision support tool","Energy efficient train operation","Quadratic optimisation","Timetabling optimisation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Cubris - A Thales Company"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a decision support tool for energy optimising railway timetables based on behavioural data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84805434/Matthias.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383101","identifier":[{"id":"85075605567","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7d206273-76a7-48fd-a8a9-fb99887672c7"],"keyword":["Data preprocessing","Decision support tool","Energy-efficient train operation","Quadratic optimisation","Timetabling optimisation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D36D46EB066914C087E5F81C5E49E287"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84805434/Matthias.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Cubris - A Thales Company"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Bejlegaard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Mathias Bejlegaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias Villads Hinsch","key":"alspau","last":"Als","name":"Als, Matthias Villads Hinsch","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sune","key":"edingergrampau","last":"Edinger Gram","name":"Edinger Gram, Sune","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-31140-7_25","isbn":["9783030311391"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"397-412","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 10th International Conference on Computational Logistics (ICCL19)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075605567"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7d206273-76a7-48fd-a8a9-fb99887672c7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Decision Support Tool for Energy-Optimising Railway Timetables Based on Behavioural Data","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383101","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Accurate Vessel Capacity Models (VCMs) expressing the trade-off between different container types that can be stowed on container vessels are required in core liner shipping functions such as uptake-, capacity-, and network management. Today, simple models based on volume, weight, and refrigerated container capacity are used for these tasks, which causes overestimations that hamper decision making. Though previous work on stowage planning optimization in principle provide finegrained linear Vessel Stowage Models (VSMs), these are too complex to be used in the mentioned functions. As an alternative, this paper contributes a novel framework based on Fourier-Motzkin Elimination that automatically derives VCMs from VSMs by projecting unneeded variables. Our results show that the projected VCMs are reduced by an order of magnitude and can be solved 20–34 times faster than their corresponding VSMs with only a negligible loss in accuracy. Our framework is applicable to LP models in general, but are particularly effective on block-angular structured problems such as VSMs. We show similar results for a multi-commodity flow problem.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ajspur, Mai Lise","Jensen, Rune Møller","Andersen, Kent Høj"],"cuid":["S02-085.71-793251"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCL","title":"International Conference on Computational Logistics"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Block Angular Structured Problems","Container shipping","Fourier Motzkin Elimination","Stowage Planning Optimization","Vessel Capacity Models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a decomposed fourier motzkin elimination framework to derive vessel capacity models","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84805455/rmj2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-085.71-793251","identifier":[{"id":"85075605211","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-53eb057d-b54c-4ba5-b065-f5f7d9fae440","itu-dce07c59-4855-4dfb-8293-d0f4cb45d8c8"],"keyword":["Block-Angular Structured Problems","Container Shipping","Fourier-Motzkin Elimination","Stowage Planning Optimization","Vessel Capacity Models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-286407F7940F0CF801B2768C691E4972"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84805455/rmj2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Mathematics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mai Lise","key":"ajspurpau","last":"Ajspur","name":"Ajspur, Mai Lise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"0f19103a-ce2a-4f57-a0f7-13506a2e241d","name":"Andersen, Kent","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-31140-7_6","isbn":["9783030311391"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"85-100","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 10th International Conference on Computational Logistics (ICCL19)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075605211"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-53eb057d-b54c-4ba5-b065-f5f7d9fae440","itu-dce07c59-4855-4dfb-8293-d0f4cb45d8c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Decomposed Fourier-Motzkin Elimination Framework to Derive Vessel Capacity Models","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-793251","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Most bacterial infections initiate at the mucosal epithelium lining the gastrointestinal, respiratory, and urogenital tracts. At these sites, bacterial pathogens must adhere and increase in numbers to effectively breach the outer barrier and invade the host. If the bacterium succeeds in reaching the bloodstream, effective dissemination again requires that bacteria in the blood, reestablish contact to distant endothelium sites and form secondary site foci. The infectious potential of bacteria is therefore closely linked to their ability to adhere to, colonize, and invade epithelial and endothelial surfaces. Measurement of bacterial adhesion to epithelial cells is therefore standard procedure in studies of bacterial virulence. Traditionally, such measurements have been conducted with microtiter plate cell cultures to which bacteria are added, followed by washing procedures and final quantification of retained bacteria by agar plating. This approach is fast and straightforward, but yields only a rough estimate of the adhesive properties of the bacteria upon contact, and little information on the ability of the bacterium to colonize these surfaces under relevant physiological conditions. Here, we present a method in which epithelia/endothelia are simulated by flow chamber-grown human cell layers, and infection is induced by seeding of pathogenic bacteria on these surfaces under conditions that simulate the physiological microenvironment. Quantification of bacterial adhesion and colonization of the cell layers is then performed by in situ time-lapse fluorescence microscopy and automatic detection of bacterial surface coverage. The method is demonstrated in three different infection models, simulating Staphylococcus aureus endothelial infection and Escherichia coli intestinal- and uroepithelial infection. The approach yields valuable information on the fitness of the bacterium to successfully adhere to and colonize epithelial surfaces and can be used to evaluate the influence of specific virulence genes, growth conditions, and antimicrobial treatment on this process.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Rune Micha","Grønnemose, Rasmus Birkholm","Stærk, Kristian","Antoinette Asferg, Cecilie","Bill Andersen, Thea","Kolmos, Hans Jørn","Møller-Jensen, Jakob","Andersen, Thomas Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-577556"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bacterial Adhesion","Bacterial Infections microbiology","Bacterial Physiological Phenomena","Cells Cultured","Epithelial Cells microbiology","Gastrointestinal Tract microbiology","Humans","Models Theoretical","Staphylococcus aureus physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a method for quantification of epithelium colonization capacity by pathogenic bacteria","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2018.00016","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-577556","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5799267","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29450193","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85041858879","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-0f4d6716-50ef-484b-9fb7-570ce17d1017"],"keyword":["Bacterial Adhesion","Bacterial Infections/microbiology","Bacterial Load/methods","Bacterial Physiological Phenomena","Cells, Cultured","Epithelial Cells/microbiology","Gastrointestinal Tract/microbiology","Humans","Models, Theoretical","Mucous Membrane/microbiology","Shiga-Toxigenic Escherichia coli/physiology","Staphylococcus aureus/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7408E8A3322B75D34989F07D2208B0AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/135558316/fcimb_08_00016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2018.00016","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Microbiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"michapedersenpau","last":"Micha Pedersen","locid":"325a072f-7766-4149-9860-e6d657e37690","name":"Pedersen, Rune Micha","name_org":"Micha Pedersen, Rune","orcid":"0000-0002-3748-055X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Birkholm","key":"grønnemosepau","last":"Grønnemose","locid":"c9ed28c9-4b29-46a2-8af9-1b6295395be6","name":"Grønnemose, Rasmus Birkholm","orcid":"0000-0001-6411-9981","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","locid":"0e1429ba-881e-4a1a-b489-bdfbbaae2599","name":"Stærk, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2410-0375","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie","key":"antoinetteasfergpau","last":"Antoinette Asferg","locid":"f0b2c8f7-6946-4fad-94e1-3f4d7eb0b2b9","name":"Antoinette Asferg, Cecilie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea","key":"billandersenpau","last":"Bill Andersen","name":"Bill Andersen, Thea","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans Jørn","key":"kolmospau","last":"Kolmos","locid":"a3b7b0c5-f328-429d-8de3-91ad1079218e","name":"Kolmos, Hans Jørn","orcid":"0000-0002-5640-953X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob","key":"møllerjensenpau","last":"Møller-Jensen","locid":"da5fc759-06a8-4643-8744-8753a77fef6b","name":"Møller-Jensen, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0002-6008-3771","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Emil","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"87fae7cd-ed6a-4d21-80cc-e13da9f91099","name":"Andersen, Thomas Emil","orcid":"0000-0001-9453-1141","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29450193"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fcimb.2018.00016","issn":["22352988"],"issue":"FEB","journal":"Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology","paperid":"16","publisher":"Frontiers Media","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85041858879"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0f4d6716-50ef-484b-9fb7-570ce17d1017"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Method for Quantification of Epithelium Colonization Capacity by Pathogenic Bacteria","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-577556","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Container Vessel Stowage Planning is the first complete textbook on stowage planning including containers, vessels, terminals, forecasts, the planning process, software tools, and automation research. It teaches you how to make winning stowage plans in a competitive market. The book is ideal for education of stowage planners, and it is a valuable reference for decision makers in higher business functions such as uptake, capacity, network, and fleet management.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Jensen, Rune Møller","Pacino, Dario","Ajspur, Mai Lise","Vesterdal, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695256"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Container Vessels","Fleet Management","Stowage Automation","Stowage planning","Terminal operations"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Sealytix"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"container vessel stowage planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-695256","ids":["itu-763aec9e-d533-4f72-9bda-d5b22c341477"],"keyword":["Container Vessels","Fleet Management","Stowage Automation","Stowage Planning","Terminal Operations"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3A513F8E7FEB920E830D86F699B31192"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l