{"abstract":"Post-operative pain is a problem for many patients and affects recovery, risk of post-operative complications and quality of life. A thorough preoperative evaluation, careful perioperative planning, identification, and individualized treatment of high-risk patients can reduce post-operative pain. Multimodal treatment combines different analgesic techniques in order to utilize synergistic and additive effects of different treatments and has the potential to optimize effects and reduce side effects. Identification and treatment of patients with chronic post-operative pain should be prioritized.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","Jensen, Jan Mick","Møller, Jytte Frandsen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621887"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Humans","Pain Management methods","Preoperative Care","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behandling af postoperative smerter","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85024385790","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-621887","identifier":[{"id":"85024385790","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28648159","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-aa0127f0-5008-46ac-8c59-02fefd7ba976"],"keyword":["Humans","Pain Management/methods","Pain, Postoperative/physiopathology","Preoperative Care","Risk Factors"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-FA560389313412FF642945A32A1DE991"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Rune","key":"blichfeldteckhardtpau","last":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt","locid":"f603c66f-99ca-4f58-984c-8a37cd15773c","name":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","orcid":"0000-0002-7759-5642","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Mick","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jan Mick","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jytte Frandsen","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Jytte Frandsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28648159"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"13","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"1151-1154","paperid":"V02170090","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"179"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85024385790"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-aa0127f0-5008-46ac-8c59-02fefd7ba976"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Behandling af postoperative smerter","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-621887","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Glucagon is secreted from pancreatic α cells, and hypersecretion (hyperglucagonemia) contributes to diabetic hyperglycemia. Molecular heterogeneity in hyperglucagonemia is poorly investigated. By screening human plasma using high-resolution-proteomics, we identified several glucagon variants, among which proglucagon 1-61 (PG 1-61) appears to be the most abundant form. PG 1-61 is secreted in subjects with obesity, both before and after gastric bypass surgery, with protein and fat as the main drivers for secretion before surgery, but glucose after. Studies in hepatocytes and in β cells demonstrated that PG 1-61 dose-dependently increases levels of cAMP, through the glucagon receptor, and increases insulin secretion and protein levels of enzymes regulating glycogenolysis and gluconeogenesis. In rats, PG 1-61 increases blood glucose and plasma insulin and decreases plasma levels of amino acids in vivo. We conclude that glucagon variants, such as PG 1-61, may contribute to glucose regulation by stimulating hepatic glucose production and insulin secretion.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Wewer Albrechtsen, Nicolai J.","Kuhre, Rune E.","Hornburg, Daniel","Jensen, Christian Z.","Hornum, Mads","Dirksen, Carsten","Svane, Maria","Gasbjerg, Lærke S.","Jørgensen, Nils B.","Gabe, Maria N.","Balk-Møller, Emilie","Albrechtsen, Reidar","Winther-Sørensen, Marie","Galsgaard, Katrine D.","Meissner, Felix","Jorsal, Tina","Lund, Asger","Vilsbøll, Tina","Eliasen, Rasmus","Bojsen-Møller, Kirstine N.","Idorn, Thomas","Deacon, Carolyn F.","Knop, Filip K.","Rosenkilde, Mette M.","Hartmann, Bolette","Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","Mann, Matthias","Madsbad, Sten","Holst, Jens J"],"cuid":["S02-096.32-035421"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute of Biochemistry"],"keyword":["Alpha cells","GLP 1","Glucagon","L cells","Proglucagon","Proteomics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"circulating glucagon 000000000001 000000000061 regulates blood glucose by increasing insulin secretion and hepatic glucose production","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2017.10.034","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.32-035421","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5695911","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85034087701","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000414541700006","type":"wos"},{"id":"29117552","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-7b511021-3b07-43b6-9570-15b792cf700d","ku-5de0f9aa-7d95-4884-a486-1ef985f758da"],"keyword":["Alpha cells","GLP-1","Glucagon","L-cells","Proglucagon","Proteomics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F42198E5AEEDBFFA70EFCDD4DFFD154A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2017.10.034","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/185994866/1_s2.0_S2211124717314663_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139517968/1_s2.0_S2211124717314663_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nord