757437577"],"issn":["2245280X"],"issue":"5","pages":"245-263","place":"København","publisher":"Djøf Forlag","series":"Studier i dansk politik","status":"p","subtitle":"Folketingsvalget 2015","title":"Oprør fra udkanten"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-34bf73a8-865e-470b-b067-eafe3aca6fbf"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Partivalg og holdninger til velfærdsstaten","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-159506","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Due to its high computational complexity, Fourier-Motzkin-Elimination (FME) is mainly known as a theoretical approach to determine feasibility of a linear program (LP). Current applications of FME in static program analysis and logic programming is based on the fact that it is a transformation corresponding to existential quantification in logic. Large-scale variable elimination, however, has to our knowledge not been attempted so far. In this report, we introduce a novel FME-based framework for massive variable elimination that takes advantage of the block structure found in many LP problems. Our objective is to simplify the LP by eliminating most of its variables. We show that this is possible for the key challenge in liner shipping of defining the capacity of container vessels as a function of the mixture of cargo they carry.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ajspur, Mai Lise","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384203"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Existential Quantification","Fourier Motzkin Elimination","Linear programming","Static Program Analysis","Variable Elimination"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using fourier motzkin elimination to derive capacity models of container vessels","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81631647/ITU_TR_2017_197.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384203","ids":["itu-c83ff2ce-821b-43d7-87b3-dcaacb5565a1"],"keyword":["Existential Quantification","Fourier-Motzkin Elimination","Linear Programming","Static Program Analysis","Variable Elimination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-95983A2340245BE7E735E466A5915AD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81631647/ITU_TR_2017_197.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mai Lise","key":"ajspurpau","last":"Ajspur","name":"Ajspur, Mai Lise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2017-197","pages":"46","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2017-197","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c83ff2ce-821b-43d7-87b3-dcaacb5565a1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using Fourier-Motzkin-Elimination to Derive Capacity Models of Container Vessels","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384203","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Causes behind low male and female fecundity have been suggested to be initiated in foetal life. However, fecundity is also affected by environmental exposures later in life, and genetic factors are known to play a role. Using survey data on Danish twins, the aim of this study was to quantify the relative contribution of genetic and environmental effects on fecundity, measured as waiting time to the first attempt to achieve a pregnancy. In 1994, a population-based survey was conducted among twins born 1953-1982. Another survey was carried out in 1998 among twins born 1931-1952. We restricted the study population to twins 18 years or older. All analyses were performed both separately for the two surveys and combined. We used a quantitative genetic liability threshold model, splitting the variation of subfertility risk into A (additive genetic effects), D (dominant genetic effects), C (common environmental effects) and E (individual environmental effects) and calculated tetrachoric correlations by zygosity. The analyses were performed both crude and univariately adjusted for age at first attempt to become pregnant, smoking, years in school, age at menarge, oral contraceptives and survey. Waiting time was included as a binary outcome, with cut point at 10 months. Based on the Akaike Information Criterion the model including dominant genetic and unique environmental factors (DE model) gave the best fit in most cases. Adjusted results for all females (746 MZ and 831 DZ twin pairs) showed that the relative contribution of dominant genetic factors to subfertility was 30% (95% CI 16-44%) and the remainder 70% (95% CI 56-84%) was explained by environmental factors specific for each twin individual, with a tetrachoric correlation of 0.30 (0.15-0.43) for MZ and 0.09 (-0.06-0.24) for DZ. For males (531 MZ and 610 DZ twin pairs), the adjusted results showed that dominant genetic factors explained 6% (95% CI 0-26%) and the remainder 94% (95% CI 74-100%) was due to unique environmental factors, with a tetrachoric correlation of 0.08 (-0.12-0.28) for MZ and -0.04 (-0.21-0.14) for DZ. All results were consistent across surveys and almost similar for the crude and adjusted models. In conclusion, our results suggest that environmental factors specific for each twin individual explained the largest part (app. 70%) of subfertility for females and almost 100% for males.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ahrenfeldt, Linda Juel","Möller, Sören","Jensen, Tina Kold","Christensen, Kaare","Lindahl-Jacobsen, Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-598544"],"event":{"end":"2017-12-18","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2017-11-16","title":"The 16th Congress of the International Society Twin Studies","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"heritability of subfertility among danish male and female twins","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-598544","ids":["sdu-586c3851-357d-462d-8300-e94428a63c68"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2FEB144201E57AA432BE8274E5C5B195"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Biodemography Unit (DEM)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Epidemiology, Biostatistics and Biodemography"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linda","key":"juelahrenfeldtpau","last":"Juel Ahrenfeldt","locid":"286f9573-a0ee-4487-b04b-ed1e883a39f5","name":"Ahrenfeldt, Linda Juel","name_org":"Juel Ahrenfeldt, Linda","orcid":"0000-0002-5018-1642","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sören","key":"möllerpau","last":"Möller","locid":"905018dc-c6c4-4a79-b50d-d0c08618e77a","name":"Möller, Sören","orcid":"0000-0003-0858-4269","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Kold","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"50e57e0b-3ce7-4b7d-9d24-125d84b7a62d","name":"Jensen, Tina Kold","orcid":"0000-0003-2311-5778","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kaare","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"35c0eca6-0f49-465b-9bbd-ce71bcf2c4ac","name":"Christensen, Kaare","orcid":"0000-0002-5429-5292","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rune","key":"lindahljacobsenpau","last":"Lindahl-Jacobsen","locid":"069d0e17-d8fd-42e8-a1bb-967bb3c54b74","name":"Lindahl-Jacobsen, Rune","orcid":"0000-0002-4622-9826","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-586c3851-357d-462d-8300-e94428a63c68"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Heritability of Subfertility Among Danish Male and Female Twins","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-598544","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Indvinding af skifergas har i de senere år påkaldt sig stigende interesse internationalt og i Danmark. På den baggrund har Miljø- og Fødevareministeriet bedt DTU, GEUS og DCE om at indgå en konsortieaftale om at udarbejde en videnskabelig udredning. Formålet med den videnskabelige udredning er at sætte international viden om indvinding af skifergas i relation til en dansk kontekst. I udredningen redegøres der for de regionale geologiske forhold i skifergasproduktion i Danmark, boring og effekt af boring og frakturering, og der foretages en analyse af de mulige påvirkninger af miljø og vandressourcer samt landskab og trafik. På den baggrund gives der indledningsvist en overordnet beskrivelse af skifergas, forventet anvendt teknologi i forbindelse med skifergasproduktion samt en beskrivelse af mulige miljøpåvirkninger og tilgængelige afværgeforanstaltninger. Den videnskabelige udredning indeholder også en screening af de risici og farer, der kunne være forbundet med skifergasindvinding i Danmark.","author_count":39,"contributors":["Nielsen, Niels Axel","Christensen, Thomas Højlund","Aagaard, Niels-Jørgen","Bach, Hanne","Larsen, Flemming","Britze, Peter","Molzen, Jan Eiersted","Hansen, Steffen Foss","Johnsen, Anders R.","Jensen, Poul Nordemann","Odgaard, Mads H","Bjerg, Poul Løgstrup","Fabricius, Ida Lykke","Jensen, Lotte Bjerregaard","Scheutz, Charlotte","Andersen, Henrik Rasmus","Kjeldsen, Peter","Hjorth, Rune","Baun, Anders","Kozin, Igor","Nikolajew, Maja Møller","Sørensen, Morten Kanne","Nielsen, Thomas Alexander Sick","Schovsbo, Niels","Kidmose, Jakob B.","Gravesen, Peter","Voss, Peter","Jakobsen, Rasmus","Pedersen, Stig Asbjørn Schack","Larsen, Tine B.","Dahl Jensen, Trine","Laier, Troels","Sanderson, Hans","Baattrup-Pedersen, Annette","Winding, Anne","Levin, Gregor","Jessen Rasmussen, Jes","Gustavson, Kim","Frederiksen, Pia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-376031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","