{"abstract":"Containerization plays an important role in the battle for the reduction of CO2 emissions in international transportation. The more containers a vessel carries, the smaller is the resulting CO2 emissions per transported ton of cargo. This suggested focus on vessel intake maximization is old news for liner shippers. Stowage managers fight this battle daily. They are the planners of the cargo and have to find a load configuration that both suits the cargo to load in the current port and in addition guarantees that the vessel can be utilized to its maximum in future ports. The size of vessels nowadays, however, is making this work harder and harder. Moreover, the cargo composition available in the different ports might not be suitable for the full utilization of the vessel. To give a very brief example, consider a vessel that has to load a high number of very heavy containers. As a consequence the draft of the vessel will be greater. If the vessel has to visit a port with a lower draft limitation, stowage managers will have to leave a number of containers behind in order to reduce the draft. In this work we use vessel stowage models to analyse how well a composition of cargo fits the stowage characteristics of a containership. Moreover, we will present the first vessel stowage model to handle variable displacement. A series of experiments will be presented showing the performance of the model and e.g. it's improved accuracy as a revenue model.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Delgado-Ortegon, Alberto","Pacino, Dario","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384622"],"event":{"end":"2015-07-15","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2015-07-12","title":"27th European Conference on Operational Research","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CO2 emissions reduction","Cargo composition analysis","Containerization","Containership stowage model","Draft limitations","Revenue model","Stowage management","Transportation efficiency","Variable displacement handling","Vessel intake maximization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the cargo composition problem","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-384622","ids":["itu-e3be0d31-291c-463b-b42d-ec64d72c6620"],"keyword":["CO2 emissions reduction","Cargo composition analysis","Containerization","Containership stowage model","Draft limitations","Revenue model","Stowage management","Transportation efficiency","Variable displacement handling","Vessel intake maximization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C585657F2CBA6CBC9C95DC04F0FBBBE1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberto","key":"delgadoortegonpau","last":"Delgado-Ortegon","name":"Delgado-Ortegon, Alberto","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dario","key":"pacinopau","last":"Pacino","name":"Pacino, Dario","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e3be0d31-291c-463b-b42d-ec64d72c6620"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Cargo Composition Problem","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384622","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Visible aggregates formed during storage in acidic whey protein isolate (WPI) dispersions represent a challenge to the beverage industry. Batch-to-batch variations are observed that prevents consistent quality and shelf-life prediction. Heat-treatment of WPI dispersions at 120°C for 20s instead of conventional heating at 95°C for 180s often prevents the aggregate formation, and varying levels of divalent cations were proposed to contribute to the observed batch-to-batch variations. In this study, the composition of the visible aggregates was examined. Caseinomacropeptide (CMP) was enriched in the visible aggregates compared with the surrounding clear liquid. Disruption of electrostatic interactions between glycosylated and non-glycosylated CMPs were studied by addition of calcium, acidification, and enzymatic de-sialidation. The treatment strategies each significantly decreased time-dependent turbidity development in acidic WPI dispersions. This suggests that the storage-induced aggregates may be prevented by disruption of electrostatic interactions between negatively-charged sialic acid residues and positively-charged amino acids.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Villumsen, Nanna Stengaard","Jensen, Hanne Bak","Le, Thao Thi Thu","Møller, Hanne Søndergård","Nordvang, Rune Thorbjørn","Ravn Nielsen, Line","Bang Nielsen, Søren","Sørensen, John","Hammershøj, Marianne","Larsen, Lotte Bach"],"cuid":["S02-096.70-015371"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Calcium","Caseinomacropeptide","Sialic acid","Whey protein","Whey protein isolate"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-ARLA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-ARLA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"