{"abstract":"AIMS: To assess the long-term mortality and occurrence of post-ablation atrial fibrillation in patients undergoing a radiofrequency ablation for the Wolff-Parkinson-White (WPW) syndrome. METHODS AND RESULTS: A retrospective cohort study of patients (N = 362) subjected to radiofrequency ablation of the WPW syndrome at Aarhus University Hospital from 1990 to 2011. A comparison cohort (N = 3619) was generated from the Danish National Board of Health Central Population Registry. We found no significant difference in all-cause mortality when comparing the WPW group with the control group [hazard ratio (HR): 0.77 and confidence interval (CI): 0.47-1.25]. After radiofrequency ablation, the WPW group had a significantly higher risk of atrial fibrillation than the control group (HR: 4.77 and CI: 3.05-7.43). Atrial fibrillation prior to ablation (HR: 4.66 and CI: 2.09-10.41) and age over 50 years (HR: 9.79 and CI: 4.29-22.36) at the time of ablation were independent risk factors for post-ablation atrial fibrillation in the WPW group. CONCLUSION: Patients with radiofrequency ablation-treated WPW syndrome have a post-ablation mortality that is similar to the background population. The risk of atrial fibrillation remains high after radiofrequency ablation of the WPW syndrome.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Borregaard, Rune","Lukac, Peter","Gerdes, Christian","Møller, Dorthe","Mortensen, Peter Thomas","Pedersen, Lars","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-264507"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"radiofrequency ablation of accessory pathways in patients with the wolff parkinson white syndrome the long term mortality and risk of atrial fibrillation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euu176","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-264507","identifier":[{"id":"84922418848","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25013013","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ecd4d7a5-8fe2-4082-9e5a-d0b428256a7d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-67B05D44DD130CFE7507BC5A196E4A37"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euu176","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune","key":"borregaardpau","last":"Borregaard","locid":"6ccde17a-fbce-4e7a-86b5-8be2c3b63bee","name":"Borregaard, Rune","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"lukacpau","last":"Lukac","locid":"fd777227-f249-49d0-a043-7fb8e56d93c1","name":"Lukac, Peter","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"gerdespau","last":"Gerdes","locid":"43704ceb-b5ba-49ac-bff8-5e26e3b9d419","name":"Gerdes, Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"b8b2d858-3f52-4e44-ba53-cd3df482f578","name":"Møller, Dorthe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Thomas","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Peter Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Cosedis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"cc1c8be7-f54a-4722-8077-aa358f9b090a","name":"Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","orcid":"0000-0001-9414-1653","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Kjærulf","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5fb8d709-1b6d-4959-8f16-a4b5d78b436d","name":"Jensen, Henrik Kjærulf","orcid":"0000-0003-1802-4302","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25013013"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/europace/euu176","issn":["10995129","10996044"],"issn_org":["10995129"],"journal":"Europace","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Europace"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84922418848"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ecd4d7a5-8fe2-4082-9e5a-d0b428256a7d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Radiofrequency ablation of accessory pathways in patients with the Wolff-Parkinson-White syndrome : the long-term mortality and risk of atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-264507","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Low-cost containerized shipping requires high-quality stowage plans. Scalable stowage planning optimization algorithms have been developed recently. All of these algorithms, however, produce monolithic solutions that are hard for stowage coordinators to modify, which is necessary in practice owing to exceptions and operational disruptions. This article introduces an approach for modifying a stowage plan interactively without breaking its constraints. We focus on rearranging the containers in a single-bay section and show two approaches for providing complete and backtrack-free decision support using symbolic configuration techniques, one based on binary decision diagrams and one based on DPLL solvers. We show that binary decision diagrams can be used to solve real-world sized instances of a single bay, and that search-based solvers can be used to solve simplified instances going beyond a single bay.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kroer, Christian","Svendsen, Martin Kjær","Jensen, Rune Møller","Kiniry, Joseph Roland","Leknes, Eilif"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384365"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University"],"keyword":["Binary Decision Diagrams","Containerized Shipping","DPLL Solvers","Interactive Decision Support","Stowage Planning Optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symbolic configuration for interactive container ship stowage planning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/coin.12051","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384365","identifier":[{"id":"84940278556","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d2cbc67e-ed95-467b-8966-ede48fbf1d75"],"keyword":["Binary Decision Diagrams","Containerized Shipping","DPLL Solvers","Interactive Decision Support","Stowage Planning Optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3CB06B9D966004507DC1ABE945DDC3B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/coin.12051","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"kroerpau","last":"Kroer","name":"Kroer, Christian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Kjær","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","name":"Svendsen, Martin Kjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph Roland","key":"kinirypau","last":"Kiniry","name":"Kiniry, Joseph Roland","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Eilif","key":"leknespau","last":"Leknes","name":"Leknes, Eilif","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/coin.12051","issn":["08247935","14678640"],"issn_org":["08247935"],"journal":"Computational Intelligence","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84940278556"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d2cbc67e-ed95-467b-8966-ede48fbf1d75"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Symbolic Configuration for Interactive Container Ship Stowage Planning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384365","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The optimization of container ship and depot operations embeds the k-shift problem, in which containers must be stowed with at most k rehandles. We first solve an open problem showing that changing from uncapacitated to capacitated stacks reduces the problem complexity from NP-complete to polynomial. We then examine the complexity of an abstraction of the current state-of-the-art container ship stowage planning, the hatch overstow problem. We show that this problem is NP-complete, which means that even abstract formulation of container ship stowage planning is intractable.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pacino, Dario","Tierney, Kevin","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380136"],"event":{"end":"2014-07-18","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2014-07-13","title":"20<sup>th</sup> Conference of the International Federation of Operational Research Societies.","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Paderborn University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the complexity of container stowage planning problems","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-380136","ids":["dtu-fc971cd6-2392-45ae-896b-f07a3587417f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DFAFF0AE2B6935107CCD9FDB5C415CC5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport, Transport optimisation and technique"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"paderborn university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Paderborn University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dario","key":"pacinopau","last":"Pacino","locid":"f5e14177-3ab5-450c-863d-5705c1712588","name":"Pacino, Dario","orcid":"0000-0002-7255-004X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"tierneypau","last":"Tierney","name":"Tierney, Kevin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fc971cd6-2392-45ae-896b-f07a3587417f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"On the Complexity of Container Stowage Planning Problems","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380136","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The optimization of container ship and depot operations embeds the kk-shift problem, in which containers must be stowed in stacks such that at most kk containers must be removed in order to reach containers below them. We first solve an open problem introduced by Avriel et al. (2000) by showing that changing from uncapacitated to capacitated stacks reduces the complexity of this problem from NP-complete to polynomial. We then examine the complexity of the current state-of-the-art abstraction of container ship stowage planning, wherein containers and slots are grouped together. To do this, we define the hatch overstow problem, in which a set of containers are placed on top of the hatches of a container ship such that the number of containers that are stowed on hatches that must be accessed is minimized. We show that this problem is NP-complete by a reduction from the set-covering problem, which means that even abstract formulation of container ship stowage planning is intractable.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Tierney, Kevin","Pacino, Dario","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S02-099.69-036488"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Computational complexity","Container Stowage","Liner shipping","Overstowage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the complexity of container stowage planning problems","src":["dtu","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2014.01.005","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.69-036488","identifier":[{"id":"84895920062","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-ac03afa0-07c3-4c38-abb5-6454472f0a21","itu-a401311e-0f11-470c-a6b9-06fb9085a0cd"],"keyword":["Computational Complexity","Container stowage","Liner shipping","Overstowage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9C1E0BAECF709A0CA29CBD3BE9A2A6C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2014.01.005","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Transport, Transport optimisation and technique"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"tierneypau","last":"Tierney","name":"Tierney, Kevin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dario","key":"pacinopau","last":"Pacino","locid":"f5e14177-3ab5-450c-863d-5705c1712588","name":"Pacino, Dario","orcid":"0000-0002-7255-004X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.dam.2014.01.005","issn":["0166218X","18726771"],"issn_org":["0166218X"],"journal":"Discrete Applied Mathematics","pages":"225-230","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Discrete Applied Mathematics","volume":"169"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84895920062"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ac03afa0-07c3-4c38-abb5-6454472f0a21","itu-a401311e-0f11-470c-a6b9-06fb9085a0cd"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the complexity of container stowage planning problems","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.69-036488","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"This book constitutes the refereed proceedings of the 4th International Conference on Computational Logistics, ICCL 2013, held in Copenhagen, Denmark, in September 2013. The 19 papers presented in this volume were carefully reviewed and selected for inclusion in the book. They are organized in topical sections named: maritime shipping, road transport, vehicle routing problems, aviation applications, and logistics and supply chain management.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jensen, Rune Møller","Pacino, Dario","Voß, Stefan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365445"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-27","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2013-09-25","title":"4th International Conference on Computational Logistics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Hamburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lecture notes in computer science including subseries lecture notes in artificial intelligence and lecture notes in bioinformatics preface","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dbp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/bfm:978-3-642-41019-2/1?pdf=chapter%20toc","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365445","identifier":[{"id":"84886391626","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cbe876b7-ed1b-4275-97b4-d7358817654f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B3ADE1E031AFC6FE6BA95EA1FBB54700"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/bfm:978-3-642-41019-2/1?pdf=chapter%20toc","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country"