{"abstract":"This book constitutes the refereed proceedings of the 4th International Conference on Computational Logistics, ICCL 2013, held in Copenhagen, Denmark, in September 2013. The 19 papers presented in this volume were carefully reviewed and selected for inclusion in the book. They are organized in topical sections named: maritime shipping, road transport, vehicle routing problems, aviation applications, and logistics and supply chain management.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Pacino, Dario","Voss, Stefan","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382437"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCL","end":"2013-09-27","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2013-09-25","title":"4th International Conference on Computational Logistics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Hamburg"],"keyword":["Aviation Applications","Computational Logistics","Maritime shipping","Supply chain management","Vehicle Routing Problems"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computational logistics 000000000004th international conference iccl 000000002013 copenhagen denmark september 000000000025 000000000027 000000002013 proceedings","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382437","ids":["itu-4e5161d6-e011-4524-b102-0faaa10d1601"],"keyword":["Aviation Applications","Computational Logistics","Maritime Shipping","Supply Chain Management","Vehicle Routing Problems"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7E177BD4626AB2E616F37A6DA9DF99D3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of hamburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hamburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dario","key":"pacinopau","last":"Pacino","name":"Pacino, Dario","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan","key":"vosspau","last":"Voss","name":"Voss, Stefan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"8197"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4e5161d6-e011-4524-b102-0faaa10d1601"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computational Logistics : 4th International Conference, ICCL 2013, Copenhagen, Denmark, September 25-27, 2013, Proceedings","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382437","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We introduce a novel, node flow based mathematical model for the fixed-time version of a central problem in the liner shipping industry called the Liner Shipping Fleet Repositioning Problem (LSFRP). We call this version of the problem the Inflexible Visitation LSFRP (IVLSFRP). During repositioning, vessels are moved between routes in a liner shipping network. Shipping lines wish to reposition vessels as cheaply as possible without disrupting the cargo flows of the network. The LSFRP is characterized by chains of interacting activities with a multi-commodity flow over paths defined by the activities chosen. We introduce two versions of a node flow based model that exploit the fixed activity times of the IVLSFRP’s graph to handle cargo demands on the nodes of the graph, instead of the arcs, significantly reducing the number of variables. Using this model in CPLEX, we are able to solve 12 previously unsolved IVLSFRP instances to optimality. Additionally, we improve the solution time on every instance in the IVLSFRP dataset, sometimes by several orders of magnitude.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Tierney, Kevin","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383431"],"event":{"acronym":"ICCL","end":"2013-09-27","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2013-09-25","title":"4th International Conference on Computational Logistics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CPLEX","Fixed Time Scheduling","Fleet Repositioning","IVLSFRP","Liner Shipping Fleet Repositioning Problem","Mathematical modeling","Multi commodity flow","Node Flow","Optimality","Shipping Network Optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a node flow model for the inflexible visitation liner shipping fleet repositioning problem with cargo flows","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-41019-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383431","identifier":[{"id":"84886391626","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-933937c1-80a5-41cb-b764-5d5e6f2b97ba"],"keyword":["CPLEX","Fixed-Time Scheduling","Fleet Repositioning","IVLSFRP","Liner Shipping Fleet Repositioning Problem","Mathematical Modeling","Multi-Commodity Flow","Node Flow","Optimality","Shipping Network Optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC15CF6B380C808DF7C4673C54783D39"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-41019-2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"tierneypau","last":"Tierney","name":"Tierney, Kevin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-642-41019-2","issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"18-34","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"8197"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886393093"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-933937c1-80a5-41cb-b764-5d5e6f2b97ba"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Node Flow Model for the Inflexible Visitation Liner Shipping Fleet Repositioning Problem with Cargo Flows","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383431","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Cargo-mix and containership stowage optimization are unknown problems to most and scientific blind spots with less than 100 publications over more than four decades. This state of affairs borders on the ridiculous, given that containerized shipping is a major driver of the global economy and still uses inefficient cargo management procedures. In this talk, Jensen will show you that these problems – in contrast to the view of publications on the topic – in realistic settings are surprisingly easy. He will outline how to generate optimal stowage plans and cargo-mixes for some of the world’s largest container vessels using standard mathematical programming techniques and off-the-shelf solvers. The presentation will provide basic insight into the domain, with pointers to further information that enable you to join in this promising new path of operations research and business.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381635"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cargo mix optimization","Containership stowage","Global shipping logistics","Mathematical programming","Operations research"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"stowing the right containers on container vessels","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381635","ids":["itu-18a7df1f-2f3d-4ea0-b30d-321cfa1d1302"],"keyword":["Cargo-mix optimization","Containership stowage","Global shipping logistics","Mathematical programming","Operations research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1C8DA4AF4FD93749B06FA6835B70ED80"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-18a7df1f-2f3d-4ea0-b30d-321cfa1d1302"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Stowing the Right Containers on Container Vessels","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381635","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Decision support systems have become a viable approach to tackle complex optimization problems. The combination of experts' know-how and efficient optimization algorithms can dramatically improve solution quality and reduce work time. Some of these systems rely on continuous interaction with their users and almost all require fast feedback from the optimization algorithms. We propose a placement heuristic that serves as the optimization component of a decision support system to interactively generate container vessel stowage plans, a complex problem with high economical impact within the shipping industry. Our experimental evaluation shows that the placement heuristic is fast enough for interactive optimization and produces solutions that are competitive with expert users.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Delgado-Ortegon, Alberto","Jensen, Rune Møller","Guilbert, Nicolas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382952"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Heuristic methods","Linear programming","Stowage planning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a placement heuristic for a commercial decision support system for container vessel stowage","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-382952","ids":["itu-71a2532e-71d2-47e2-946d-3b6ed60d2f6f"],"keyword":["Heuristic methods","Linear Programming","Stowage planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66379B76E87860484219784C5731F76D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3