{"abstract":"Eco-Efficient stowage plans that are both competitive and sustainable have become a priority for the shipping industry. Stowage planning is NP-hard and is a challenging optimization problem in practice. We propose a new 2-phase approach that generates near-optimal stowage plans and fulfills industrial time and quality requirements. Our approach combines an integer programming model for assigning groups of containers to storage areas of the vessel over multiple ports, and a constraint programming and local search procedure for stowing individual containers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pacino, Dario","Jensen, Rune Møller","Delgado-Ortegon, Alberto","Bebbington, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381731"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South"],"country":["Singapore"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Maersk Line Operations, Global Stowage Production"],"keyword":["Constraint programming","Eco efficient stowage plans","Integer programming","NP hard problems","Shipping industry optimization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast generation of near optimal plans for eco efficient stowage of large container vessels","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/80054077216","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381731","identifier":[{"id":"80054077216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-1f482ed6-f99f-4380-ad81-34472e0a2e77"],"keyword":["Constraint programming","Eco-efficient stowage plans","Integer programming","NP-hard problems","Shipping industry optimization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C79E5788D26E97B9E1CA00ADC3B0F304"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sg","key":"maersk line operations global stowage production","loc":["Singapore","Asia, South"],"name":"Maersk Line Operations, Global Stowage Production","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dario","key":"pacinopau","last":"Pacino","name":"Pacino, Dario","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberto","key":"delgadoortegonpau","last":"Delgado-Ortegon","name":"Delgado-Ortegon, Alberto","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tom","key":"bebbingtonpau","last":"Bebbington","name":"Bebbington, Tom","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783642242632"],"pages":"286-301","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"ICCL (2011). Proceedings of the International Conference on Computer Languages"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80054077216"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1f482ed6-f99f-4380-ad81-34472e0a2e77"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fast Generation of Near-Optimal Plans for Eco-Efficient Stowage of Large Container Vessels","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381731","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Liner shipping fleet repositioning consists of moving vessels between services in a liner ship- ping network in order to better orient the overall network to the world economy, and to ensure the proper maintenance of vessels. Thus, fleet repositioning involves sailing and loading activities subject to complex handling and timing restrictions. The objective of the problem is cost minimization, which translates nearly directly into the minimization of CO2 emissions and pollution. Additionally, it is important that all cost elements, including the ones that are only loosely coupled with activity choices, can be accurately modeled. Numerous liner shipping fleet repositioning problems are solved each year by the world’s shipping firms without the assistance of any decision support, even though humans can require between two to three days to find a reasonable solution. Finding optimal repositionings is important in helping shipping firms move towards their goal of greater eco-efficiency.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Tierney, Kevin","Jensen, Rune Møller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384432"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cost minimization","Decision support systems","Eco efficiency","Fleet Repositioning","Liner Shipping Network"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"liner shipping fleet repositioning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/32276876/iccl2011_top.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-384432","ids":["itu-d7205c06-ece9-4668-b434-410b48b3c5e5"],"keyword":["Cost Minimization","Decision Support Systems","Eco-Efficiency","Fleet Repositioning","Liner Shipping Network"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-B1644DF39D0E3174D6EF84B9601C1544"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/32276876/iccl2011_top.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://gauss.econ.uni-hamburg.de/iccl2011/submission.html","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"tierneypau","last":"Tierney","name":"Tierney, Kevin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rune Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"4d7fda5a-3cf4-4d39-9daf-1ae192b0e0e7","name":"Jensen, Rune Møller","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d7205c06-ece9-4668-b434-410b48b3c5e5"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Liner Shipping Fleet Repositioning","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384432","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Eco-efficient stowage plans that are both competitive and sustainable have become a priority for the shipping industry. Stowage planning is NP-hard and is a challenging optimization problem in practice. We propose a new 2-phase approach that generates near-optimal stowage plans and fulfills industrial time and quality requirements. Our approach combines an integer programming model for assigning groups of containers to storage areas of the vessel over multiple ports, and a constraint programming and local search procedure for stowing individual containers.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pacino, Dario","Delgado, Alberto","Jensen, Rune Møller","Bebbington, Tom"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340637"],"event":{"end":"2011-09-22","place":"Hamburg, de","start":"2011-09-19","title":"2nd International Conference on Computational Logistics","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computer","Operations","Ship"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-MAE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-MAE","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast generation of near optimal plans for eco efficient stowage of large container vessels","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/54505047/Fast_generation_of_near_optimal_plans_for_eco_efficient_stowage_of_large_container_vessels.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340637","identifier":[{"id":"80054077216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-78d2fe28-ca35-4801-a2d7-d6a5d27e71d5"],"keyword":["COMPUTER","OPERATIONS","SHIP"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0F60B516D15AF4533FB06D91EC639945"],"oa_link":[{